// Ch15 B14 side scene (optional): "Two Daces" (E, 4 min, ~200 words). act2_ch15.md §4. The dock-master's
// hull-house at supper, an oil lamp's hiss the only sound. He puts a second bowl on the table without
// asking. He doesn't talk about his son: grief in this house is work and bowls. Two men who knew two
// different Daces. RULES: no line names the ship or says why Dace left (Ch17's ledger); the reasons never
// fully excuse him. Liss comes in halfway with the lamp if Rhen sat with her on the barge.
title: ch15_two_daces
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@camera H15
@anim aldous_varrow set_bowl rhen
@wait 3.0
<<if $ch11_rhen_admitted>>
    Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Liss says you're Sallow's boy. #line:ch15_daces_001
<<else>>
    Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: You're Sallow's boy. I can see it. #line:ch15_daces_002
<<endif>>
Rhen [neutral]: Yeah. #line:ch15_daces_003
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: You've got his hands. Wright's hands. Don't let the diving fool you. #line:ch15_daces_004
@wait 2.0
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [soft_smile]: He came through here twenty years ago trading salvage. Could hear a current in the water before he saw it. #line:ch15_daces_005 #long
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [soft_smile]: Sang every chart he knew. Too loud. #line:ch15_daces_006
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Came back years after. Built a hull in my dry-dock for a season, left it half-done, never came back for it. Best ear in the flotilla. Worst at finishing things. #line:ch15_daces_007 #long
<<if $ch15_sat_with_liss>>
    @mark liss supper walk
    @anim liss sit_beside rhen
    @anim aldous_varrow set_bowl liss
    @wait 2.0
<<endif>>
Rhen [sad]: He hummed the same song every night. Came home off the wrecks with salt in his beard. #line:ch15_daces_008
Rhen [sad]: Went up the coast for wall-work when I was eight. Didn't come back. #line:ch15_daces_009
Rhen [neutral]: He left his lantern on its hook. That's the one thing he finished. #line:ch15_daces_010
@wait 3.0
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [sad]: He never said he had a son. Not once. #line:ch15_daces_011
@wait 2.0
<<if $ch14_spoke_with_tobin>>
    Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [sad]: You talked to my boy. Before. What did he say? #line:ch15_daces_013
    Rhen [tender]: He said nobody had to be chosen. He volunteered. #line:ch15_daces_014
    @wait 3.0
<<endif>>
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Now I know why he never finished anything here. #line:ch15_daces_012
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch15_supper_with_father = true>>
===
